# Java Javadocs

- Add Javadocs to every Java class, interface, enum, record, and nested type you create or modify.
- Add Javadocs to every non-boilerplate method you create or modify.
- Skip constructors plus plain getters, setters, `toString()`, `equals()`, and `hashCode()` unless they contain non-obvious behavior.
- Keep docs concrete: explain the type or method responsibility, important inputs, return values, side effects, and failure behavior when relevant.
- For test files, add brief Javadocs to the test class and each test method describing the behavior being verified.
- Do not add filler comments; if the code is obvious, keep the Javadoc short.
